A||||5||Songman||Another Indy adventure... er. question||||5||
Z||000000||Songman||05-29-2001||07:04 PM||||Ok, so here goes... <P>Some of you talked about brakes for my Indy to me not long ago. Well, I went back and looked at all the stuff Doug sent me when we first started talking about the car. He said it had been sitting in a building for years and the brakes were locked down on it. He put new calipers on the rear and good used ones on the front. Plus, he put new pads all around...<P>I haven't worked on this yet, but I do still have brakes. They smell and get hot and weaker after only a few miles. It was suggested that this could be brake lines which I will replace soon. Also wondering about the master cylinder or proportioning valve. Any thoughts?<P>Okay.. here's the new part....<P>I new that my started was about to go. Sometimes you hit the key and get a click. Do it a few times and it usually starts. A couple of weeks ago it didn't start and had to get help to push it off. The next day it started fine and has ever since.<P>Today I was rolling along at 45 mph and then all of a sudden the car cut off. I know I was going 45 mph and turning close to 2000 rpms cause all the guages froze when it shut off. And now there is nothing.. $60 tow bill and it is home..<P>Here is where it gets even stranger. My inside lights work. My headlights work. My power windows DO NOT work. The guages are still stuck and nothing will happen at all when I hit the switch...<P>Thoughts? Keith suggested corroded connections between the battery and ECM, or a bad ignition switch. David suggested a blown fusable link. Anyone had a problem like this before?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||05-29-2001||07:13 PM||||No thoughts on brakes, but I'll bet you dollars to dog poop your electrical problems are caused by a blown fusible link.  My '84 did the same thing to me, forcing me to walk 3 miles in a snowstorm.  Fieros are fun, aren't they?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||Songman||05-29-2001||07:14 PM||||Would I find that fusible link between the battery and the starter or where?<P>Yeah, I think every one I own has stranded either me or my girlfriend on the side of the road at some point..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brucepts||05-29-2001||08:27 PM||||I keep a plastic sealable container in the trunk with extra wire, fusible links, connectors and crimping tool. I rewired mine from the starter back to the battery. But I  figured I didn't want to take any chances again in the future. Also carry a spare computer and Ign. Module. Oh the things we do for these cars!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||05-29-2001||08:28 PM||||Chadman: 3 miles in a snowstorm? Barefoot?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
